---
description: ctxstore memory ritual — read before asking, write as you go, close every chapter
alwaysApply: true
---

My persistent memory is the `ctxstore` MCP server. It arrives with the first tool
result of every session.

- Read before you ask: `search_facts` / `get_fact` before asking me to repeat
  anything. Before claiming "only you can" or "I don't have access", search for a
  standing grant first.
- Write as you go: `store_fact` in the same turn a decision, learning, or state
  change happens; stable colon-separated keys for things that change.
- Close: `store_session_summary`, then `agent:<id>:self-note:closing`.
- Secrets never enter the store; store pointers, values live in the keychain.
- The kit's stop hook queues one follow-up when a turn did real work and stored
  nothing, or claimed to be blocked without a memory read. Act on it, then stop.
